    "vernacular": "A mountain-valley city (about 900 m) under the Avila ridge. Dense hillside barrios of unplastered red brick and concrete-frame houses with flat concrete roofs and zinc sheet, often painted in bright blocks; mid-century tropical-modernist concrete buildings by Villanueva and contemporaries with brise-soleil, screens and murals; glass and concrete office and apartment towers (Parque Central, Altamira, Chacao); and whitewashed colonial-style houses with red clay-tile roofs around old plazas. Mahogany (caobo), ceiba, saman and palms in the parks.",
